550	
551	- **Declaration-like getters** (state refs, one-expression deriveds):
552	  contiguous within their group — a `get x() { return ref(0) }` is morally
553	  a field, and fields read as a struct-like table you absorb at a glance.
554	  The GROUP is the unit, not the member.
555	- **Blank line the moment a member carries a doc comment or multi-line
556	  logic** — comments and paragraphs of code need air.
557	- **Blank line + `// --- section ---` banner between categories**
558	  (state → derived → methods) — the boundary that actually matters.
559	- **Methods: always separated** — they are paragraphs, not table rows.
560	
561	Not machine-enforceable (linters can't tell a ref-getter from a method, and
562	Prettier expands getters past the single-line exemptions) — hold it as a
563	convention and check it in review.
564	
565	## Self-review checklist (run over your ivue diff)
566	
567	- [ ] Every mutable state member is `get x() { return ref(...) }` — no mutable plain fields.
568	- [ ] Inside the class, every Ref/Computed read/write uses `.value`; plain fields are constants/config only.
569	- [ ] Derived values are PLAIN getters; `computed()` appears only for expensive / render-suppressing / stable-handle cases.
570	- [ ] Stores/composables are injected via `private get $store() { return useStore() }`, not field initializers.
571	- [ ] The class is exported through the namespace (`$Class` / `Class = Reactive($Class)` / `Instance`); generics cast `Class` and hand-apply `ReactiveInstance` to `Instance<T>`.
572	- [ ] The SFC does `new X.Class(...)` once — no `reactive()` wrapper, no unwrap view.
573	- [ ] The SFC destructures ALL template-touched Refs/Computeds + element refs (grouped: state refs / computed refs / element refs); templates use state bindings and dotted access ONLY for plain getters/methods — no Ref reached through the instance in a template, no state name shadowing a prop.
574	- [ ] Nothing but Refs/Computeds/element-ref targets is destructured (never plain getters/methods); v-for item cells stay dotted with `.value`; instance-swapping components don't destructure at all.
575	- [ ] `defineExpose(x as X.Instance)`; consumers type the ref as `ShallowUnwrapRef<X.Instance>`.
576	- [ ] Watch sources are the FUNCTION form; component-scoped constructors use plain `watch`/`watchEffect`; `this.$watch`/`this.$watchEffect` only for component-outliving instances — each with a dispose path (`$stopEffects()` owner or `onScopeDispose` auto-wire).
577	- [ ] Lifecycle hooks / init logic live in the constructor (no `init()` expecting auto-call); template refs guarded with `?.` where read pre-mount.
578	- [ ] Every `computed()`/constructor-watch CALLBACK delegates to a method (`computed(() => this.recalculate())`) — no logic inlined in reactive closures; the arrow form, never `computed(this.method)`.
579	- [ ] Identifiers are unfolded to domain words (`row`/`col`/`cell`/`cellValue`/`versionRef`…), loop indices and specs included — no single-letter names, no name meaning different things in different methods.
580	- [ ] Keyed/sparse state uses the Map-of-refs shape (get-or-create on read, peek-only bump on write, explicit release path) — never one getter per key, never a deep `reactive()` collection.
581	- [ ] Spacing carries meaning: declaration-like getters contiguous within their group; blank lines only where a doc comment / multi-line body / category boundary begins; methods always separated.
